WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.890
Wash, condition, stretch and detangle before braiding.

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.250
This is the video for module 2 of Hair Care and Simple Styling.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:17.840
Neat, long-lasting braids start before the first part. The hair must be clean, conditioned, and detangled without breaking strands.

4
00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:29.890
It must also be stretched, because coily hair shrinks as it dries, and fully dry before extensions go in. Damp hair sealed inside braids dries very slowly.

5
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.680
Many home salons have no basin. Two buckets are enough.

6
00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:42.900
Bucket A holds lukewarm water. Mix hot into cold, never the other way round, and test it on the inside of your wrist.

7
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:47.440
Bucket B sits under her head to catch the rinse water.

8
00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:53.440
Have a jug, a spray bottle, a cape, a neck towel and a dry towel ready.

9
00:00:54.690 --> 00:01:04.640
Keep everything in reach so you never leave her with wet hair. Heat water away from the wash area, never with wet hands, and keep cables away from water and feet.

10
00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:14.210
Coily hair tangles when it is scrubbed in one big mass. So first divide the dry hair into 4 to 6 sections and twist each one.

11
00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:19.510
Wet one section at a time, letting the water run into Bucket B.

12
00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:26.950
Put a small amount of shampoo on the scalp only, and work it with the pads of your fingers, never your nails.

13
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:38.120
Rinse until the water runs clear and the hair no longer feels slippery. Leftover product can make the scalp itchy under braids. Then condition the length.

14
00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:45.660
Finally, wrap the hair in a towel to absorb water. Do not rub it, because rubbing damages hair.

15
00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:52.480
For example, Bisi runs a home salon in Ibadan and wants to know what a wash costs her.

16
00:01:53.730 --> 00:02:04.290
A 500 ml bottle of shampoo costs about 4,500 naira. One wash uses about 20 ml, so that is 180 naira.

17
00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:12.410
Conditioner at about 5,000 naira for 500 ml, using 30 ml, is 300 naira.

18
00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:18.500
Two jerrycans of water at about 100 naira each is 200 naira.

19
00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:28.260
That is about 680 naira in materials, before her time. Prices are approximate, so measure your own usage with a marked cup.

20
00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:43.440
You can stretch with heat. Blow-dry damp, not dripping, hair on the lowest heat that works, with a heat protectant, moving the dryer from root to ends. If the hair smells burnt or the ends feel crispy, the heat is too high.

21
00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:56.790
Or use African threading: wrap soft thread down each section and leave it to dry overnight. It is gentle on fine hair. If she feels tightness at the root, unwind and wrap more loosely.

22
00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:06.630
Detangling is where most salon damage happens. Work on damp hair with a conditioner or detangler that gives slip, and a wide-tooth comb.

23
00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:11.470
Take a section no wider than your palm and clip the rest away.

24
00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.070
Separate it gently with your fingers first.

25
00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:26.040
Hold the hair firmly a little above where you comb. Comb the last few centimetres first, then move up a little at a time until the comb glides from root to tip.

26
00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:36.570
The commonest mistake is combing a section that has dried and shrunk. Keep the spray bottle at hand. And big sections hurt more and break more hair.

27
00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:51.750
When braids come out, clients are often shocked by the loose hair. Explain calmly. Shed hair cannot fall out while braided, and shedding 50 to 100 hairs a day is normal. A shed hair has a small white bulb.

28
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:59.250
Short pieces with no bulb are breakage. Write that on her card, especially if it comes from the edges.

29
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:05.600
Remove the shed hair with your fingers before you wet it, or the water mats it into knots.

30
00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:20.570
To remember. Test the water on your wrist. Wash in sections. Blot, never rub, and dry fully before braiding. Stretch with low heat or threading. Detangle damp hair in small sections, from the ends up.

31
00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:25.460
With tender heads and children, take breaks and book more time instead of rushing.

32
00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:39.320
Now practise. Time a full wash and work out your material cost. Compare blow-drying and threading on two halves of one head. Then time a detangle and sort the shed hair from the broken pieces.

33
00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.610
Continue with the lessons below.
